## Authentication
Cookie-based (abconvert-session) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Data Read (5)
- `GET /{id}` — Retrieve data for a specific item by ID.
- `GET /custom-fonts/api/v1/company-fonts/onsite` — Get a list of company fonts available on the site.
- `GET /forms/api/v7/UXzVXV/full-forms` — Fetch the full form data for a specific form.
- `GET /pagead/conversion/{conversionId}/` — Retrieve conversion data for a specific conversion ID.
- `GET /store/cymatics-fm.myshopify.com/2020-12/{2020-12Id}` — Get data for a specific Shopify store item.

### Data Write (4)
- `POST /.well-known/shopify/monorail/unstable/produce_batch` — Send a batch of data to Shopify Monorail.
- `POST /event` — Submit a generic event.
- `POST /unstable/produce_batch` — Send a batch of data (unstable).
- `POST /v1/{v1Id}` — Post data to a specific endpoint (v1).

### Media (1)
- `GET /cdn/shopifycloud/storefront/assets/storefront/{storefrontJwt}` — Download a storefront asset using a JWT.

### Realtime (1)
- `POST /event/v1/events` — Send a real-time event.

### Config (1)
- `GET /config/api/v1/cymatics-fm/subscriber/config/widget/` — Get the widget configuration for subscribers.

## Quick Start

Here are some quick examples to get you started with the `cymatics-fm` API:

```typescript
